; galena-dns local allowlist (RPZ)
;
; This zone is loaded FIRST, ahead of every blocklist, because in RPZ a PASSTHRU
; is itself a match — and a match stops unbound evaluating any later policy zone.
; So anything listed here wins outright over all three blocklists.
;
; Hagezi publishes no RPZ allowlist (there is no such file in their rpz/
; directory), so this file is yours to maintain. Edit it here in the repo and
; re-run `make deploy`; never edit it on the node.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Owner names are RELATIVE to the zone apex. That is not a typo and not a bug:
; RPZ encodes the trigger as <trigger>.<zone-apex>, so a bare "example.com"
; below is exactly how you allow example.com. Do not add a trailing dot.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; To allow a domain (and, separately, its subdomains):
;
;     example.com            CNAME rpz-passthru.
;     *.example.com          CNAME rpz-passthru.
;
; To allow an IP ADDRESS — needed when the response-IP threat zone
; (tif-ips.txt) has a false positive, e.g. a shared CDN address. The format is
; prefixlength.reversed-octets.rpz-ip, so 203.0.113.42/32 becomes:
;
;     32.42.113.0.203.rpz-ip CNAME rpz-passthru.
;
; ...and a whole /24, 203.0.113.0/24, becomes (note: only the covered octets,
; still reversed):
;
;     24.0.113.0.203.rpz-ip  CNAME rpz-passthru.
;
; For IPv6 the form is prefixlength.reversed-groups.rpz-ip with zero-compression
; written as a doubled separator, e.g. 2001:db8::1/128:
;
;     128.1.zz.db8.2001.rpz-ip CNAME rpz-passthru.
;
; After editing, `make deploy` reloads this zone. To check it took effect:
;     unbound-control auth_zone_reload allowlist.rpz.galena
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$TTL 3600
@   SOA localhost. root.localhost. 1 3600 600 86400 3600
@   NS  localhost.

; --- TEST FIXTURE -----------------------------------------------------------
; analytics.google.com is present in the adblock blocklist, so allowing it here
; proves in a single query that passthru beats the blocklists and that zone
; order is correct. `make test` asserts it returns NOERROR.
;
; It is here ONLY for that test. Delete both lines if you do not want this
; domain reachable through your resolver — `make test` will then report the
; allowlist check as SKIP rather than failing.
analytics.google.com    CNAME rpz-passthru.
*.analytics.google.com  CNAME rpz-passthru.
; --- end test fixture -------------------------------------------------------

; --- Your allowlist entries below ------------------------------------------
